# Sites still outside sprout_str_word, sprout_ptr_word and the ADDRESS_CASTS functions, one
# `file:decl:count` per line, sorted.  A site is a pointer-to-integer cast, or a uintptr_t/intptr_t
# value converted to a signed 64-bit integer that is not itself such a cast's result.  The list
# only shrinks: `just runtime-word-casts` fails on a new entry, a higher count, or an entry whose
# decl now has fewer sites (lower or delete it).  After a conversion, regenerate with
#   python3 -I scripts/runtime_word_casts.py clang runtime /dev/null runtime/ADDRESS_CASTS --emit-baseline
